From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
Subject: [PATCH] sparc32: take node 0 as the root node in the romvec
 property operations

The property operations of the OpenBoot 2.x romvec (no_proplen,
no_getprop, no_nextprop) take node 0 for the root node. The Solaris 2.3
kernel asks for the root's "name" that way when it creates the root of
its device tree (and boots under the SS-5's own PROM). OpenBIOS answered
-1, and Solaris 2.3 allocated a buffer of that size and panicked with a
data fault at 0xfffff000 right after its banner.

Look node 0 up as the root node (the peer of node 0) in those operations.
---
 arch/sparc32/romvec.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/sparc32/romvec.c b/arch/sparc32/romvec.c
index ca653a4..435b905 100644
--- a/arch/sparc32/romvec.c
+++ b/arch/sparc32/romvec.c
@@ -65,10 +65,21 @@ int obp_child(int node)
     return child;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The property operations of the OpenBoot 2.x PROMs take node 0 for the root
+ * node: the Solaris 2.3 kernel asks for the root's "name" that way when it
+ * creates the root of its device tree.
+ */
+static int obp_propnode(int node)
+{
+    return node ? node : obp_nextnode(0);
+}
+
 int obp_proplen(int node, const char *name)
 {
     int notfound;
 
+    node = obp_propnode(node);
     if (!node) {
         DPRINTF("obp_proplen(0x0, %s) = -1\n", name);
         return -1;
@@ -115,6 +126,7 @@ int obp_getprop(int node, const char *name, char *value)
     int len;
     const char *str;
 
+    node = obp_propnode(node);
     if (!node) {
         DPRINTF("obp_getprop(0x0, %s) = -1\n", name);
         return -1;
@@ -176,6 +188,7 @@ const char *obp_nextprop(int node, const char *name)
 {
     int found;
 
+    node = obp_propnode(node);
     if (!name || *name == '\0') {
         // NULL name means get first property
         push_str("");
